Paste the following acceptance-criteria checklist into ENG-410:

Checkout flow:
- Single-page checkout replaces 3-step flow and completes the full purchase without page navigation or redirects; 
- Guest checkout completes order without account creation and logged-in users can select or edit saved addresses with auto-suggest that populates the address form; 
- Address form enforces client-side validation and blocks submission until all required fields pass validation

Payments:
- Only credit/debit card payments supported at launch and cards are tokenized client-side before sending to the payment API; 
- Invalid card data shows field-level error copy and prevents submission; 
- On successful payment the UI shows order confirmation and a transaction ID, and failed payments show the specified payment error copy

Shipping & pricing:
- On entering or changing ZIP/postcode the client calls the shipping service and displays shipping cost and delivery estimate in the order summary; 
- Taxes, discounts, shipping, and order total recalculate immediately when address, shipping option, or coupon inputs change and the updated totals are visible before final submission

UI & errors:
- Order summary is sticky on desktop and collapsible on mobile and always displays current line items, taxes, shipping, discounts, and total; 
- Inline, field-level errors display per spec copy; top-of-page error banner appears only for system-level failures; 
- Form submission is blocked while any field-level validation errors exist

Performance & telemetry:
- Page achieves First Interactive < 2.5s on 3G in our standard performance test harness and all third-party scripts load async; 
- Telemetry emits events for view, address entered, shipping selected, payment submitted, and order confirmed, and logs error types and validation failure rates; 
- Feature is behind a feature flag and able to run at 10% traffic for rollout with metrics-based ramp/rollback controls
